* ALWAYS ADD HELPER METHODS TO CACHE QUERIES AND AGGREGATIONS FOR BUSINESS LOGIC, RELYING ON $appends WHEN FITTING;
* For Log:: calls that log exceptions, ALWAYS LOG THE LINE AND FILE OF THE EXCEPTION FOR EASIER DEBUGGING;
* Assinging unique slugs or unique fields SHOULD ALWAYS RELY ON DO/WHILE LOOPS WITH ATTEMPT LIMITS TO AVOID INFINITE LOOPS IN EDGE CASES, following this pattern (exemplified with slugs):
while (DB::table($m->getTable())->where('slug', $candidateUrl)->where('id', '!=', $m->getAttribute('id') ?? '')->exists());